@ruanformigoni 
Sounds awesome! Do you have an idea where this is in the pipeline? No rush or anything, just curious.

Thanks for the info!

@TellSackett

Thanks for the attempt and while it probably would work for certain images I think the idea of being able to store the image within the flat image as a full cd image is better. There is also the problem that by extracting the data from the cd any games that have mixed mode CDs will lose all cd audio that way. 
Cdemu is the only way I have seen in Linux to mount the image fully with data and audio

@ruanformigoni 

I am looking forward to the new version, by the way, take into consideration to add the Proton UMU. which is the ultimate proton with very high compatibility.

Thanks for your work.

@ruanformigoni 

Is it possible to make flatimages in the future locally without depending on internet?

Keep the good work, and nice to see you're here again.
